From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 02:49:53 +0200
Subject: media: hm5065: Allow the raw bus format to be overridden

Raw output works but arrives as two bytes per pixel: ten bits of data in
a sixteen bit container, high byte first, values spanning 0 to 1023. The
ISP downstream takes eight bits per pixel, so this is not yet usable by
it, and a 2592 pixel line occupies 5184 bytes where the capture expects
2592.

Register 0x7000 selects byte and component order across sixteen values.
Which of them gives one byte per pixel, if any does, has to be found by
trying them: the vendor never used raw on this part and its own raw
format table is empty.

It cannot be swept from userspace. Writing 0x7000 while the sensor is
streaming stalls it -- measured, the frame never arrives -- and outside
streaming the chip is powered down and will not answer an I2C read. So
take it as a parameter instead, and let one build cover the search.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c | 21 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
@@ -533,6 +533,23 @@ static const struct hm5065_pixfmt hm5065_formats[] = {
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * Raw arrives as two bytes per pixel, ten bits of data in a sixteen bit
+ * container, and the ISP downstream can only take eight. Register 0x7000
+ * selects byte and component order over sixteen values and the vendor
+ * never used it for raw, so which of them gives one byte per pixel -- if
+ * any does -- has to be found by trying them.
+ *
+ * It cannot be swept from userspace: writing 0x7000 while the sensor is
+ * streaming stalls it, and outside streaming the chip is powered down and
+ * will not answer. Hence a parameter, so that one build covers the search.
+ * Negative means use the value from the format table.
+ */
+static int raw_bus_format = -1;
+module_param(raw_bus_format, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(raw_bus_format,
+		 "override register 0x7000 for raw formats (-1: table default)");
+
 static bool hm5065_format_is_raw(const struct hm5065_pixfmt *fmt)
 {
 	return fmt->data_fmt == HM5065_REG_DATA_FORMAT_RAW10ITU8 ||
@@ -1698,7 +1715,9 @@ static int hm5065_setup_mode(struct hm5065_dev *sensor,
 	cci_write(map, HM5065_REG_YCRCB_ORDER, pix_fmt->ycbcr_order, &ret);
 	/* without this, brightness, contrast and saturation will not work */
 	cci_write(map, HM5065_REG_COLORSPACE, 9, &ret);
-	cci_write(map, HM5065_REG_BUS_DATA_FORMAT, pix_fmt->fmt_setup, &ret);
+	cci_write(map, HM5065_REG_BUS_DATA_FORMAT,
+		  hm5065_format_is_raw(pix_fmt) && raw_bus_format >= 0 ?
+		  raw_bus_format : pix_fmt->fmt_setup, &ret);
 	cci_write(map, HM5065_REG_DESIRED_FRAME_RATE_NUM, fps, &ret);
 	cci_write(map, HM5065_REG_DESIRED_FRAME_RATE_DEN, 1, &ret);
 
